# AI Learning Journey – Micah

This repository documents my ongoing journey learning software development and AI. 
I studied through LaunchCode’s curriculum and spent about a year following MIT’s 
Introduction to Computer Science lectures on YouTube, practicing along with the material 
and building a foundation in programming logic and problem-solving.

Even though I didn’t complete a full application, I focused on understanding how code 
works, how AI models process information, and how to break problems down into smaller 
steps. This repo represents the beginning of my hands-on learning.

Included in this project:

- Simple Python demo scripts
- Practice exercises and logic experiments
- A roadmap of future projects I plan to build
- Ideas for expanding into AI, automation, and beginner software development

This repository is a snapshot of my learning progress and a starting point for building 
real projects as I continue exploring AI and software development.
